{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fyrrxjih6gbrxt73rd7y2mt36ciy566zhlrjjjcxveclfvmihpuq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01AxBCvTDJisSCNqy64tnTqV","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-9wooaB/translated_rust/tests/differential_descriptors.rs","old_string":"extern \"C\" {\n    fn pipe(fds: *mut i32) -> i32;\n    fn close(fd: i32) -> i32;\n}\n\nfn make_pipe() -> (OwnedFd, OwnedFd) {\n    let mut fds = [0i32; 2];\n    assert_eq!(unsafe { pipe(fds.as_mut_ptr()) }, 0, \"pipe(2) failed\");\n    unsafe { (OwnedFd::from_raw_fd(fds[0]), OwnedFd::from_raw_fd(fds[1])) }\n}","new_string":"extern \"C\" {\n    fn pipe2(fds: *mut i32, flags: i32) -> i32;\n    fn close(fd: i32) -> i32;\n}\n\n/// `O_CLOEXEC` is essential here: these tests run on several threads at once,\n/// and a plain `pipe(2)` would leak its ends into children spawned by *other*\n/// threads between `pipe` and `drop(r)`. An unrelated child holding the read\n/// end keeps the pipe readable, so the expected `SIGPIPE` never arrives and the\n/// test flakes. `Stdio::from` still works, because the descriptor is `dup2`ed\n/// onto the child's stdio (which clears `FD_CLOEXEC` on the copy).\nfn make_pipe() -> (OwnedFd, OwnedFd) {\n    const O_CLOEXEC: i32 = 0o2_000_000;\n    let mut fds = [0i32; 2];\n    assert_eq!(\n        unsafe { pipe2(fds.as_mut_ptr(), O_CLOEXEC) },\n        0,\n        \"pipe2(2) failed\"\n    );\n    unsafe { (OwnedFd::from_raw_fd(fds[0]), OwnedFd::from_raw_fd(fds[1])) }\n}"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1688,"cache_read_input_tokens":165136,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1688,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"579baa65-7da4-4f36-aeb9-da13c